{
  "file": "common childhood",
  "page": 48,
  "blocks": [
    {
      "bbox": [
        113.12979888916016,
        27.289522171020508,
        340.4130554199219,
        35.34652328491211
      ],
      "text": "RECOMMENDATIONS FOR MANAGEMENT OF COMMON CHILDHOOD CONDITIONS",
      "font": "Helvetica-Condensed-Ligh",
      "size": 7.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        60.173309326171875,
        376.11102294921875,
        73.36231231689453
      ],
      "text": "5.9\t Prevention of hypothermia immediately after birth in low birth",
      "font": "Helvetica-Condensed-Bold",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        90.70860290527344,
        73.17330932617188,
        155.17959594726562,
        86.36231231689453
      ],
      "text": "weight infants",
      "font": "Helvetica-Condensed-Bold",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        89.79890441894531,
        399.03289794921875,
        103.28890228271484
      ],
      "text": "Low birth weight (LBW) neonates weighing > 1200 g who do not have complications",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        102.79890441894531,
        399.0328063964844,
        116.28890228271484
      ],
      "text": "and are clinically stable should be put in skin-to-skin contact with the mother soon",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        115.79890441894531,
        377.4829406738281,
        129.28890991210938
      ],
      "text": "after birth and after drying them thoroughly to prevent neonatal hypothermia.",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        131.20361328125,
        255.10281372070312,
        145.12362670898438
      ],
      "text": "(Strong recommendation, low quality evidence)",
      "font": "MinionPro-BoldIt",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        147.4682159423828,
        399.04290771484375,
        160.95822143554688
      ],
      "text": "In making the recommendation, the panel noted that although the plastic wraps",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        160.4682159423828,
        399.06292724609375,
        173.95822143554688
      ],
      "text": "for LBW infants are beneficial in reducing hypothermia, the possible risks of using",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        173.4682159423828,
        399.0528564453125,
        186.95822143554688
      ],
      "text": "plastic wraps in settings in developing country were not known. There is very little",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        186.4682159423828,
        399.1528015136719,
        199.95822143554688
      ],
      "text": "experience with this intervention in developing countries and further research into",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        199.4682159423828,
        399.0728759765625,
        212.95822143554688
      ],
      "text": "the type of plastic to be used, as well as the practicality and appropriateness of using",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        212.4682159423828,
        313.29290771484375,
        225.95822143554688
      ],
      "text": "the plastic-wrap technique in low-resource settings, is required.",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        236.98680114746094,
        231.48292541503906,
        248.976806640625
      ],
      "text": "5.9.1\t Evidence and summary of findings",
      "font": "Helvetica-Condensed-Bold",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        252.6414031982422,
        399.11285400390625,
        266.13140869140625
      ],
      "text": "We identified one recent systematic review through Cochrane [McCall 2010] that",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        265.6413879394531,
        399.1629333496094,
        279.13140869140625
      ],
      "text": "sought to assess the effect on interventions to prevent hypothermia in preterm and/or",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        278.6413879394531,
        399.0928649902344,
        292.13140869140625
      ],
      "text": "LBW infants. The review included three interventions of interest: (1) plastic wraps; (2)",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        291.6413879394531,
        399.062744140625,
        305.13140869140625
      ],
      "text": "plastic caps; and (3) skin-to-skin contact. Studies were included that evaluated these",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        304.6413879394531,
        399.09295654296875,
        318.13140869140625
      ],
      "text": "interventions started within 10 minutes of birth. Hypothermia was defined as core",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        317.6413879394531,
        399.1229248046875,
        331.13140869140625
      ],
      "text": "body temperature < 36.5 °C on admission to neonatal intensive care unit (NICU) or",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        330.6413879394531,
        399.1130065917969,
        344.13140869140625
      ],
      "text": "up to 2 hours after birth. There was low to moderate quality evidence that caps or",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        343.6413879394531,
        399.08282470703125,
        357.13140869140625
      ],
      "text": "plasticwraps reduced hypothermia, and moderate quality evidence that skin to skin",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        309.8953857421875,
        356.42138671875,
        387.3753662109375,
        370.13140869140625
      ],
      "text": "GRADE table A7.7",
      "font": "MinionPro-Semibold",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        356.6413879394531,
        390.7434997558594,
        370.13140869140625
      ],
      "text": "contact significantly reduced hypothermia in LBW newborns ( )",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        68.03150177001953,
        369.6413879394531,
        399.131591796875,
        383.13140869140625
      ],
      "text": "Plastic wraps or bags were effective in reducing heat loss in infants < 28 weeks’",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        382.6413879394531,
        399.0726013183594,
        396.13140869140625
      ],
      "text": "gestation (four studies; n = 223; WMD 0.68 °C; 95% CI 0.45, 0.91), but not in infants",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        395.6413879394531,
        399.06292724609375,
        409.13140869140625
      ],
      "text": "between 28 to 31 weeks gestation (1 study, n = 41). Two of the studies in infants of",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        408.6413879394531,
        399.0329284667969,
        422.13140869140625
      ],
      "text": "gestational age < 29 weeks showed that plastic wrap significantly reduces the risk of",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        421.6413879394531,
        399.102783203125,
        435.13140869140625
      ],
      "text": "hypothermia on admission to the NICU (two studies, n = 152; RR 0.66, 95% CI 0.51,",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        434.6413879394531,
        399.1227111816406,
        448.13140869140625
      ],
      "text": "0.84; RD -0.27; 95% CI -0.41, -0.13 ). Four infants would need to be wrapped in plastic",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        447.6413879394531,
        393.62274169921875,
        461.13140869140625
      ],
      "text": "in order to prevent one infant from becoming hypothermic (NNT 4, 95% CI 2 to 8).",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        68.03150177001953,
        460.6413879394531,
        399.1014404296875,
        474.13140869140625
      ],
      "text": "Plastic caps were effective in reducing heat losses in infants < 29 weeks’ gestation",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        473.6413879394531,
        399.0026550292969,
        487.13140869140625
      ],
      "text": "(one study; n = 64; MD 0.80°C; 95% CI 0.41, 1.19). This study also reported that",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        486.6413879394531,
        399.0528259277344,
        500.13140869140625
      ],
      "text": "plastic caps significantly reduce the risk of hypothermia on admission to the NICU",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        499.6413879394531,
        399.0228576660156,
        513.1314086914062
      ],
      "text": "(RR 0.48, 95% CI 0.32, 0.73; RD -0.47; 95% CI -0.67, -0.27). Two infants would need to",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        512.641357421875,
        399.142822265625,
        526.13134765625
      ],
      "text": "wear a plastic cap in order to prevent one infant from becoming hypothermic (NNT",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        525.641357421875,
        125.14289855957031,
        539.13134765625
      ],
      "text": "2, 95% CI 2 to 4).",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        68.03150177001953,
        538.641357421875,
        399.0714416503906,
        552.13134765625
      ],
      "text": "For infants with a birth weight between 1200 and 2199g, evidence suggests that",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        551.641357421875,
        399.08270263671875,
        565.13134765625
      ],
      "text": "skin-to-skin contact significantly reduces the risk of hypothermia (as defined by",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        564.641357421875,
        399.0428771972656,
        578.13134765625
      ],
      "text": "the study) within 6 hours of birth when compared to conventional incubator care",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        577.641357421875,
        398.95281982421875,
        591.13134765625
      ],
      "text": "(one study; n = 31; RR 0.09, 95% CI 0.01, 0.64; RD -0.56, 95% CI -0.84, -0.27). Two",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        590.641357421875,
        399.07281494140625,
        604.13134765625
      ],
      "text": "infants would need to receive skin-to-skin contact in order to prevent one infant",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        603.641357421875,
        272.1429138183594,
        617.13134765625
      ],
      "text": "from becoming hypothermic (NNT 2, 95% CI 1 to 4).",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        222.36920166015625,
        644.9403076171875,
        230.67620849609375,
        655.2992553710938
      ],
      "text": "34",
      "font": "Helvetica-Condensed-Ligh",
      "size": 9.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    }
  ]
}